{"name":"Cod Grey","hex":"#2d3032","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cod","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Cocama."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various types of sea fish or the meat from said fish.","A sea fish of the family Gadidae which are sold as \"cod\", as haddock (Melanogrammus aeglefinus), and whiting (usually Merlangius merlangus).\n A sea fish of the genus Gadus, inclusive of Atlantic cod (Gadus morhua), Pacific cod (Gadus macrocephalus), and Greenland cod (Gadus ogac or Gadus macrocephalus ogac).\n An Atlantic cod (Gadus morhua)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cod"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cod","blocks":[{"text":"Cod is the common name for the demersal fish genus Gadus, belonging to the family Gadidae. Cod is also used as part of the common name for several other fish species, and one species that belongs to genus Gadus is not commonly called cod."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Gadus_morhua_Cod-2b-Atlanterhavsparken-Norway.JPG/330px-Gadus_morhua_Cod-2b-Atlanterhavsparken-Norway.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cod"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_cont